# ---------- WINDOWS POWERSHELL / CMD ----------

# Go to folder containing:
# 1. mykey.pem
# 2. gardeningwebsitetemplate.zip

cd Downloads

# Check files
dir

# Upload ZIP file from Windows to EC2
scp -i mykey.pem gardeningwebsitetemplate.zip ubuntu@PUBLIC-IP:/home/ubuntu/

# Connect to EC2 Ubuntu Server
ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@PUBLIC-IP



# ---------- UBUNTU EC2 COMMANDS ----------

# Update packages
sudo apt update

# Install Apache Web Server
sudo apt install apache2 -y

# Start Apache
sudo systemctl start apache2

# Enable Apache on boot
sudo systemctl enable apache2

# Check Apache status
sudo systemctl status apache2

# Install unzip utility
sudo apt install unzip -y

# Check uploaded ZIP file
ls

# Extract ecommerce template
unzip gardeningwebsitetemplate.zip

# Copy website files to Apache directory
sudo cp -r gardeningwebsitetemplate/* /var/www/html/

# Restart Apache
sudo systemctl restart apache2

# Open Apache web directory
cd /var/www/html

# List deployed website files
ls

1. What is EC2?

EC2 is a virtual server provided by AWS used to run applications in the cloud.

2. What is Apache?

Apache is a web server software used to host websites on a server.

3. Why do we use Apache in this experiment?

To host and serve web pages over HTTP protocol.

4. What is SCP command?

SCP is used to securely transfer files from local system to remote server.

5. What is SSH?

SSH is a secure protocol used to connect to remote servers.

6. What is Security Group?

It is a virtual firewall that controls inbound and outbound traffic of EC2.

7. Why do we use port 80?

Port 80 is the default port for HTTP web traffic.

8. What is unzip command used for?

It is used to extract compressed ZIP files.

9. What is /var/www/html?

It is the default directory where Apache stores website files.

10. Why do we restart Apache?

To apply changes made in website files.

11. What is t2.micro instance?

A free-tier EC2 instance used for learning and basic applications.

12. What happens after copying files to /var/www/html?

The website becomes live and accessible via browser using public IP.

13. What is AWS?

AWS is Amazon Web Services providing cloud computing services like servers, storage, and databases.
